      "claim": "In historical and economic scholarship the phrase “crisis of the 1970s” refers to the macro‑economic downturn of that decade, i.e., stagflation, oil‑price shocks, falling corporate profits and rising unemployment.",
      "evidence": "Texts such as James K. Galbraith’s *The Crisis of the 1970s* (1979), the OECD’s 1975 report on “the crisis of the 1970s”, and standard macro‑economic histories (e.g., Blinder & Rudd, *The Economics of the 1970s*) all label the period a “crisis” on these economic grounds.",
