      "id": 2,
      "claim": "Declining profits and rising unemployment are the two hallmark indicators of that economic crisis.",
      "evidence": "Empirical data from the 1970s show corporate profit margins fell sharply after the 1973 oil shock (U.S. corporate profits fell 15% 1973‑75) while unemployment in major industrial nations rose from ~5% to >9% by 1975.",
      "weight": 0.30,
      "depends_on": [1]
    },
